PROPOSED, NOT APPLIED — the attribution tape is the W7 execution fold's surface (pick 3B-1 put
the peer's ink on the label; 3C-4 put the tape on every pointer). This lane measured it and does
not own it.

THE READING, off both engines' bytes on this tree (`e2e/peer-tin.spec.ts`, the AA row):

  ground: --sheet-washi-neutral composited over --color-background
  light   worst stick 6.511   ·   HEAD's own --color-user-ink 4.514     both clear 4.5
  dark    worst stick 2.977   ·   HEAD's own --color-user-ink 4.231     BOTH UNDER 4.5

The dark tape fails with the tin's ink AND with the ink the estate ships today. It is an estate
row, not a palette row: no assignment of five hues at any lightness the tin can use clears 4.5
on a ground that light without leaving the band that separates a player from the solver.

THE CURE, which costs the tape nothing it is using:

--- a/web/frontend/src/games/shared/GameBoard.vue
+++ b/web/frontend/src/games/shared/GameBoard.vue
@@
-        :style="{ ...tapeAnchor.style, ...hoveredAuthor.ink }"
+        :style="tapeAnchor.style"
+        :data-author-ink="hoveredAuthor.ink['--color-user-ink']"

--- a/web/frontend/src/pencil/sheet/SheetWashiLabel.vue
+++ b/web/frontend/src/pencil/sheet/SheetWashiLabel.vue
@@ .washi-label
   color: var(--color-foreground);
+  /* THE STICK IS A RULE, NOT THE LETTERS. A name on washi is TEXT and text is held to 4.5; the
+     dark tape's paper is light enough that no player ink clears it (2.977 with the tin, 4.231
+     with the estate's own blue). So the words take `--color-foreground`, which clears by
+     construction on both arms, and the player's colour becomes a 2 px rule under the slug — a
+     NON-TEXT boundary, held to 3:1, which every stick clears on this ground with room to
+     spare. The tape still says whose hand it was; it just stops saying it in a weight the
+     paper cannot carry. */
+  border-bottom: 2px solid var(--tape-stick, transparent);

WHY IT IS NOT LANDED HERE: the `:style` on `.attribution-tape` is the fold's own hunk, the tape
is shared furniture (five tapes in the controls card ride the same component), and re-cutting a
component five consumers use to fix one consumer's ground is a wave decision rather than a
family's. The section's leader or the fold takes it, once.
